    <title lang="fr">Journeys in India</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Amritsar, Shimla and Manali: The Far North</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">The Golden Temple is the centerpiece of the city of Amritsar, and probably the second most photographed building in India, but few know about the building or the people who built it. The most significant building to people of the Sikh faith, it is open to people of all faiths. We witness the celebration of the changing of the guard before heading into the mountains for a visit to the British influenced town of Shimla. Journeys then heads further north for look at the resort area of Manali.</desc>
