    <title>Winchester Life</title>
    <desc>Melissa Bachman has made her name over the last two decades as one of the most dedicated hunters and producers in the outdoor industry. In this episode we’ll tag along with Melissa while she chases big game around the world with her Winchester in hand. First we’ll head to Colorado as Melissa spot and stalks giant mule deer, then we’ll head across the pond to New Zealand to chase mountain ibex and tar, then head back to the states for Montana whitetail at ground level.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261012103000 +0000" stop="20261012110001 +0000">
    <title>Winchester Life</title>
    <desc>Shotgun sports are experiencing unprecedented growth, with competitions across the country gaining popularity as enthusiasts vie to be the best shooters in the world. Every summer, the Amateur Trapshooting Association hosts The Grand American in Sparta, Illinois. This year marks the 125th Anniversary for the largest trap shooting competition in the world. We’ll talk with the people who make this tournament run behind the scenes and explore what makes this tournament such a special event. We’ll also look at the rich history of The Grand. On-site we’ll chat with the curator of the Trapshooting Hall of Fame and look at some of the incredible historical pieces on display in the museum. Additionally, we’ll learn about White Flyer and how the clay manufacturer has made important innovations for the shotgun sports.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261012110001 +0000" stop="20261012113001 +0000">
    <title>Winchester Life</title>
    <desc>Nobody chases the waterfowl migration as hard as Shawn Stahl of Team Winchester. The Michigan native spends over half of his year running the highways and flyways searching for the x. In this episode, we’ll tag along with Shawn and his crew with their Winchester pumps in hand as they hunker down hiding in fields and timber in hopes of locked wings from ducks and geese.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-5fd115b8b7ef8d002dcf1817" start="20261012113001 +0000" stop="20261012120001 +0000">
    <title>Winchester Life</title>
    <desc>Overview: East Alton, Illinois is the home of Winchester Ammunition and the manufacturing home of the shotshell plants that build and produce millions of rounds of ammo for hunters, sport shooters, military and law enforcement. Get an unprecedented inside look at the birth cycle of a shotshell inside the walls of Winchester. From hull to primer, shot to wad and packaging to shipping, watch how the most legendary and successful ammunition brand in the world comes to is born and built.</desc>
  </programme>
  
